WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.069
Fans have been waiting years to find out which
new twists would be added to the story by

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:07.470
the new creative team for the rebooted Hellboy
franchise.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.219
We're gritting our teeth, dusting off our
tomes of BPRD history, and casting a spell

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:16.890
of blood magic to bring you all the small
details you missed in the 2019 version of

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:17.640
Hellboy.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.790
Hellboy starts the movie heading to Mexico
to find a missing B.P.R.D. agent and close

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.030
friend, Esteban.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.910
He finds his old pal wrestling in a lucha
libre arena under the name Camazotz, seemingly

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.020
indifferent to Hellboy's concern.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.699
In the comic storyline Hellboy in Mexico,
Hellboy teams up with a group of 1950s luchadores

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:38.910
while fighting vampires in Mexico.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.039
After a night of heavy drinking, one of the
brothers, Esteban, wanders out into the night

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:46.730
and gets turned into a vampiric luchador called
Camazotz.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:51.030
The movie closely follows the storyline, as
Hellboy is forced to battle against the giant

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.929
bat creature, impaling him on a ring post.

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:58.240
The movie even includes the months-long drinking
bender that Hellboy goes on afterwards.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.319
When Hellboy gets picked up by B.P.R.D. agents
in Mexico, Professor Broom lets him know he

00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:07.770
has to go to the Osiris Club to help them
out with a giant problem that they're having.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:13.680
"The British occult society born in 1866 by
the ranking members of the Heliopic Brotherhood

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.560
of Ra."

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.480
“Ra?”

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.600
In the comics, the Heliopic Brotherhood is
a group of supernatural-obsessed cultists

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.000
who went around causing trouble.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.990
They usually battled against Sir Edward Grey,
the Witchfinder, a Victorian-era precursor

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.100
to latter-day heroes like Lobster Johnson
and Hellboy.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.390
The Brotherhood's reference in the film isn't
just to show that the new film is firmly enmeshed

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.900
within the larger Hellboy comics universe.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.400
It's also a sly bit of foreshadowing to the
Osiris Club's betrayal of Hellboy while on

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.640
the Wild Hunt.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.760
If you've got a phobia of eye trauma, stay
away from this movie.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.400
Hellboy himself blinds at least three different
monsters on-screen.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:55.270
Plus, there's Baba Yaga, the witch who lost
one eye to Hellboy before the movie's events.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.530
She's eager to pop one of Big Red's yellow
eyes into her socket.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:03.580
She offers Hellboy a deal for information
on Nimue the Blood Queen's next move in return

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.090
for one of his eyes.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.209
Hellboy accepts, but ends up reneging on the
deal, telling the witch that she can have

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:10.950
the eye when he's done with it.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.859
That might not have been the right decision.

00:02:12.859 --> 00:02:16.970
He gets hit with a nasty curse and ends up
losing out on some knowledge.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.840
Hellboy probably should have remembered the
Norse myth of Odin, who is said to have traded

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.000
an eye for divine wisdom.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.360
Hellboy is able to get out of the trade with
Baba Yaga by telling the witch that she never

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:29.599
specified a time frame to collect his eye.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.909
It's a savvy trick that gives our hero the
high ground for not staying true to his word

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:38.280
when making a deal with a child-killing cannibal
witch, and it also subtly connects Hellboy

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.389
to Nimue.

00:02:39.389 --> 00:02:43.959
A significant portion of the film is devoted
to Hellboy struggling with his dual loyalties

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:49.469
to humanity - epitomized by Professor Broom
- and monsterdom, represented by Nimue.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.760
She tells him that they're bound by fate.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.019
That might be true, but they're also bound
by how tricky they both are.

00:02:56.019 --> 00:03:00.629
After Gruagach defeats Hellboy in combat,
Nimue takes the former's power away.

00:03:00.629 --> 00:03:05.250
When Gruagach reminds Nimue that she promised
to "make him whole," she responds that she

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.250
did.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.840
She just didn't tell him for how long.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.400
Nimue and Hellboy's dual trickery connects
the two characters.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.240
When Hellboy leaves her house with both his
eyes, Baba Yaga curses him that he'll use

00:03:16.249 --> 00:03:20.189
both of his eyes to see the one person he
loves most in the world suffer and die.

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:24.230
Later in the film, Alice is hit by one of
Nimue's poisonous needles, and her outlook

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.430
seems grim.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.879
With Alice knocking on Heaven's door, it seems
like the film is setting her up to be the

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:31.439
unfortunate recipient of Baba Yaga's curse.

00:03:31.439 --> 00:03:35.219
But all she needed was a little Merlin magic
to get back up on her feet.

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:41.040
The curse's real target seems to be Professor
Broom, who Nimue kills while Hellboy watches.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.599
The Wild Hunt is another element of the movie
straight out of European myths.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:49.609
There are many, many variations of the myth,
but one of the most consistent aspects of

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:53.610
the Hunt is that it presages an outbreak of
war or plague.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.620
The Wild Hunt of Hellboy is a bit distinct
in that everyone involved in the Hunt, except

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.549
for Hellboy, is a normal human.

00:03:59.549 --> 00:04:03.599
Nimue is known for bringing with her plagues
and destruction, and there are definitely

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:07.520
enough demons and soldiers milling about in
the final scenes to qualify as a war.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.600
One of the most memorable lines is when Hellboy
rebuffs Nimue's offer of romantic alliance

00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:13.769
by telling her that,

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:19.720
"This is not gonna work, ya know, cuz I’m
a Capricorn and you're f---ing nuts!"

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.500
It's not actually accurate, though.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.870
In the comics, Hellboy's given birthday is
October 5, which would make him a Libra.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.120
It's easy to see why screenwriter Andrew Cosby
went with the Capricorn; the zodiac symbol

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.250
is a goat.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.900
Hellboy's demon father takes the form of a
goat, occasionally, and Hellboy's horns are

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.600
goat-like.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.440
One of the Huntsmen asks Hellboy what his
rocky right hand is used for.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.669
"It smashes things real good."

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:48.961
That line might have come as a shock to super
fans of the comics and 2004's Hellboy, since

00:04:48.961 --> 00:04:53.780
they know that Hellboy's "Right Hand of Doom"
is the key to controlling the Ogdru-Jahad,

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.670
Lovecraftian creatures from beyond space and
time.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.819
None of that plays into 2019's Hellboy, largely
because his space-worm controlling stone hand

00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:04.379
isn't part of the movie's doomsday prophecies.

00:05:04.379 --> 00:05:09.020
It's more of a battle between his demonic
evil and Arthurian good twin heritages, with

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:13.000
the forces of evil kept decidedly in the folklore
and hellish realms.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.909
While Hellboy's appearance on a small Scottish
island after a Nazi ritual is kept fairly

00:05:17.909 --> 00:05:21.819
faithful to the original comics, there is
one noticeable twist.

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:26.020
In the original comic, the Torch of Liberty,
a creation of John Byrne's that was loaned

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.289
to Mike Mignola on a one-time basis, is there.

00:05:29.289 --> 00:05:33.331
Since the character figured so prominently
in Hellboy's origin, you'd expect him to make

00:05:33.331 --> 00:05:38.509
another appearance, but due to copyright issues,
Mignola has steered away from ever reusing

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:39.509
the Torch.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:43.020
In the movie, the pulp hero who's there is
Lobster Johnson.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.860
Whenever Mignola and his collaborators needed
to use a pulp hero to fight Nazis in the Hellboy

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.760
universe, they used the Lobster.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.479
Making him an official witness to Hellboy's
arrival on Earth is a pretty declarative statement

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:57.460
that the film takes place within that larger
universe.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.780
More importantly, they kept his catchphrase:

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:03.800
"Beware my claw, for I've come to inflict
justice!"

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:08.190
The filmmakers are clearly trying to reboot
the Hellboy franchise with this movie, and

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:12.610
they wanted to avoid audiences confusing it
for a sequel, so a lot of familiar faces from

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.740
the previous films don't appear.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.849
Yet if the ending of the film is any indication,
they knew that they could only get in one

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:22.169
movie without Hellboy's good friend Abe Sapien.

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:24.699
"Hey, Abe!"

00:06:24.699 --> 00:06:29.690
Played by Doug Jones in Hellboy and Hellboy
II: The Golden Army, Abe Sapien is an icthyo

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:32.889
sapien, a more humanoid Creature from the
Black Lagoon.

00:06:32.889 --> 00:06:38.850
The closing scene of 2019's Hellboy features
Hellboy, Alice, and Ben Daimio raiding a warehouse

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.789
in Siberia with a tank that reads "Icthyo
Sapien."

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:46.480
If the film ends up earning a sequel, it's
a sure bet Abe will appear.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.320
Hellboy's post-credits scene finds the half-demon
getting prodigiously drunk at his father's

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:55.000
grave, only to be interrupted by the Lobster's
ghost.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:59.060
Hellboy geeks out at meeting his childhood
hero, and the Lobster gives a stirring pep

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.750
talk to get Hellboy back on his feet.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.110
If there's one thing that Hellboy loves doing,
it's getting drunk with ghosts.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.110
"Oi!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.460
I need some ID, love."

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.630
"Are you serious?"

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:11.440
In fact, that's how The Wild Hunt storyline
in the comics starts.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.520
Hellboy's called to lead the Hunt after going
on a boozy tour of Great Britain's finest

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.620
ghost houses.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.680
Some character beats are simply too important
for any adaptation to ignore.

